			<div class="content" id="post-content-2443427">
									

<p>Fact: Putting ghosts inside something automatically makes it 87% cooler.</p>
<p>Thanks to EmberTech, Some_Potato, ribby, A_Random_Day, TyGently, and l33tr for reviewing this while it was a draft. If I missed your name, give me a poke.</p>
<p>I may add a photo to this at a latter date, depending on whether I can get a CC photo of a fluorescent lightbulb still in its packaging. As it is though, I feel that it can stand on its own just fine without a photo.</p>
<p>Also, since a lot of people apparently missed this, let me clarify that these lightbulbs work by electrocuting ghosts. The reason the Class-A ectomorphs are a hazard is because they're pissed off about being tortured. The reason it's only the Class-A ectomorphs that are a hazard is because they're the only ones that have sapiency and agency, making them the only ones that can want, plan, and take revenge.</p>

