														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2443493">
									

<p>Much of the dryness is intentional. It's not a super interesting anomaly, it doesn't do anything crazy. But it does give an insight into how the Foundation deals with anomalous items that don't pose enough of a threat to normalcy to justify expending anything more than a minimal amount of resources on.</p>
<p>Many of the GOIs, by their existence, imply that there is a semi-open market for anomalous items. My take on this is that the Foundation and the GOC allow some amount of open trading of anomalous items, as long as they don't threaten normalcy. This is easier than trying to clamp-down on the market, as it keeps things in a place where they can monitor.</p>
<p>What this is, in essence, is an investigatory report for a defective product. But instead of lead paint in children's toys, it's angry ghosts inside lightbulbs.</p>

